{"kind":"request","text":"Decision requested for R1 continuation 84658ea0 (source-only design; no implementation or runtime).\n\nARTIFACTS_CONFIG.registerScope pins only a ScopeId. platform(named) supports historical native code and does not define the deployed current cohort. Recommend an explicit reviewed cohort/creation-edge policy selected from the exact configured register's verified APPLIED genesis and exact native pin, never a maximum version, role/name label, caller claim, or rootOf result. rootOf follows causal authority to a signed actor and is not register ancestry. readNativeBirth accepts refused genesis as negative evidence, so lineage must separately require decision=applied at every ancestor.\n\nPlease confirm the concrete deployed pin cohorts that this policy must admit, including Grow and Lending, and whether any supported historical cohort remains intentionally admissible. Source ARCHIVE_DEVICE_APPLICATION_COHORT is register17/directory16/membership8/rules10/destination12. Lending runbook contains historical APPLICATION_COHORT register5/directory5/membership4/rules3/destination2 and newer application-publication instructions register9/directory8/destination4; these source records are not current hosted readback, so builder must not guess the actual deployed root's cohort. A verified configured-root genesis should select only the explicitly approved policy.\n\nRecommend edges verified by exact current creator birth pin plus exact sealed creator send: full ScopeRef/incarnation, entry fact hash/canonical bytes, send ordinal, exact seed and create message, seed.creator and source.at equality, then repeat through the creator's own applied birth/creator edge until the configured register. Reject broken/wrong-root/refused/unsupported-pin chains before child binding.idFromName/get. Protect every production internal deliver entry via a single namespace/binding wrapper; checking inside ScopeObject.deliver is too late for constructor SQLite/schema effects. Existing local/test ALLOW_OPEN_CREATION=true bypass remains explicit; parentless directories stay refused in deployed closed mode.\n\nDeclared children should be admitted only through actual verified creation edges from the admitted cohort, with the exact declared digest and native Directory's authenticated installed-definition closure, followed by the ordinary receiver's existing full genesis judgment. A declared label, mutable summary/current role map, or unverified supplied declaration is not lineage proof. Do you adopt this closure policy rather than banning all declared descendants or treating them as native labels?\n\nFor archived creator sends, recommend no network/archive/caller-anchor or source() fallback. Require exact proof bytes (possibly a separately bounded native read of the authenticated retained creator-edge copy already held by the child's applied genesis); validate FactUse content plus fact/hash/identity. If neither exact own bytes nor such retained proof is available within the one original run budget, fail closed before child lookup/write, and report unavailable. Please confirm whether initial slice may refuse such unavailable archived chains, or whether a bounded retained-edge RPC is mandatory for currently deployed archived descendants. Existing proofSource reads own entries only, and nativeBirth currently returns only genesis proof, so retained-copy support is not already provided.\n\nRecommend one shared bounded attempt (not a new allowance per hop): bounded body bytes/count, visits, cycles and one monotonic deadline, using existing exact-proof sender admission. Exact numerical lineage budget is a serving decision to review, not an existing requirement; current GenesisProof bounds are16 bodies/1MiB/64attempts/512visits/10s but its causal-root algorithm must not be reused. Witnesses must include actual approved Grow+Lending native/declared descendants, another register, broken/hash/ordinal/message/incarnation mismatch, refused ancestor, unsupported cohort, cycle/limit/timeout/archived missing proof, and target binding.get plus state-write sentinels. No implementation, Source publication or runtime requested by this message.","body":{"conditions":"Confirm explicit deployed cohort/edge and declared-child policy plus archived-edge availability requirement; design only, no Git artifact or implementation owed by this decision request.","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}